{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DarknessTimeAndDeath","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Time, Light, and Death","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/fuse(_:after:autostart:perform:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/daemon(_:autostart:perform:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startFuse(_:after:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopFuse(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/fuseRemaining(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startDaemon(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopDaemon(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/isDaemonActive(_:)"],"anchor":"Time-Light-and-Death"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Four mechanics turn a collection of rooms into a game with stakes: darkness the player must bring light into, timed events that move the world along whether or not the player acts, the classic SAVE \/ RESTORE \/ UNDO \/ RESTART meta-verbs, and death that offers a way back. This article covers all four — they interlock, and the Zork-style burning lantern chased by a grue uses every one of them."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Darkness-and-light-sources","text":"Darkness and light sources"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A location declared ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/dark","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" has no light of its own:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let cellar = Location {","    name(\"Cellar\")","    description(\"A low, dirt-floored cellar.\")","    dark","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the dark, the player sees “It is pitch black. You can’t see a thing.” instead of a room description, and the room’s scope collapses: its contents and exit doors stop being resolvable nouns. Carried items stay usable — you can always fumble with what’s in your hands."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An item declared a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/lightSource","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" can push the darkness back:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let lantern = Item {","    name(\"brass lantern\")","    lightSource          \/\/ can hold light; starts unlit","}","","let torch = Item {","    name(\"burning torch\")","    lightSource","    startsLit            \/\/ begins the game lit","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The player operates light sources with the built-in verbs — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"turn on lantern"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"light lantern"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"turn off lantern"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"extinguish"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"douse"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"blow out"},{"type":"text","text":" (both particle orders parse: "},{"code":"turn lantern on","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" works too). Turning a light on in a dark room prints the revealed room in the same turn; turning the only light off announces the darkness. Rules can flip the state directly through ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isLit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" — the raw setter changes only the light, announcing nothing.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A room counts as lit when it has light of its own ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/isLit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"‘s setter grants or removes exactly that) or when a lit light source’s light "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"reaches"}]},{"type":"text","text":" it:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"carried by the player (lighting only the room the player is in),"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"lying in the room, or sitting on a surface in it (however deeply stacked),","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"inside a container in the room — if the container is open or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transparent"},{"type":"text","text":". A closed opaque chest swallows the light; a shut glass box passes it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/isLit"},{"type":"text","text":" answers the whole question — “is there light here, from anything” — which is also what a rule like a grue daemon wants to know. There is no separate “always burning” trait: make a torch inextinguishable by refusing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".turnOff"},{"type":"text","text":" in a rule."}]},{"anchor":"Fuses-and-daemons","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Fuses and daemons"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent"},{"type":"text","text":" is a named timer declared in a game or bundle "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timers"},{"type":"text","text":" block. A "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"fuse"}]},{"type":"text","text":" fires once, a declared number of turns after it is started; a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"daemon","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" runs at the end of every turn while active:"}]},{"code":["var timers: [TimedEvent] {","    fuse(\"lanternDies\", after: 25) {","        lantern.isLit = false","        say(\"The brass lantern flickers and goes out.\")","    }","    daemon(\"grue\", autostart: true) {","        guard !player.location.isLit else { return }","        try die(\"You are devoured by a grue.\")","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Rules start and stop timers by name: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startFuse(_:after:)"},{"text":" (the optional count overrides the declared one; restarting resets it), ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopFuse(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/fuseRemaining(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startDaemon(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopDaemon(_:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/isDaemonActive(_:)"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"autostart","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" covers timers that should run from turn one with no starting rule. Naming a timer no ","type":"text"},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block declares is a wiring error and traps; declaring two timers with one name is a fatal bootstrap diagnostic (timer names are global across the game and its bundles — a bundle’s own rules refer to them by the literal string, so they are deliberately not namespaced).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Timers tick ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"once per typed command","type":"text"}]},{"text":", at the very end of the turn — after the world’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after"},{"type":"text","text":"\/each-turn rules, fuses first and then daemons, each group in name order. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take all"},{"type":"text","text":" over five objects ticks once, not five times. They tick on refused turns (world time passes) but not on parse errors, meta commands, or once the game has ended. A timer started during a turn ticks at the end of that same turn, so a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fuse(after: 1)"},{"type":"text","text":" started by a rule fires as that very turn ends."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"schedule"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — which timers are running, and the fuses’ remaining counts — lives in the world’s state. The bodies are code, registered at bootstrap; a restored save re-binds its schedule to the declared bodies by name. That split is what lets timers survive save files."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Save-restore-undo-restart","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Save, restore, undo, restart"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Four engine-level meta verbs manage the game as a program. Like all meta intents they run no rules and cost no turn — and they are deliberately not overridable through a game’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actions"},{"text":" block.","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"save"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" asks “Save to what file?” and writes the whole world state — placements, the turn counter, the timer schedule, the random stream, everything — as JSON to the answered path. Relative paths resolve against the current directory; an empty answer cancels.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"restore","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" asks for a filename, validates the file (a save from a different game is refused with its own message), and swaps the saved state in. Because the random stream rides along, a restored game replays exactly the randomness it would have had.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"undo","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" reverses exactly one turn, from a snapshot the engine takes before every turn that actually runs. One level, classic-style; the snapshot lives outside the world state, so undo history never leaks into save files.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"restart","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rewinds to the pristine opening — same seed, so a restarted game is the identical game — and replays the intro."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The filename prompts are round-trips through the normal input loop: the driver ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/REPL","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IOHandler"},{"type":"text","text":") never knows a question is open, which also means a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ScriptedIOHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" transcript can script "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"save"},{"type":"text","text":", the path, and the reply like any other lines."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Death — and the way back","anchor":"Death-and-the-way-back","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/end(won:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" finishes the game outright. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/die(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is the other ending: it kills the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"player","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" but keeps the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"program","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" alive."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["poison.before(.take) {","    try die(\"Ill-advised. The world goes dark.\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The engine prints the message, the death banner, and the score, then offers the classic choice:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["*** You have died ***","","Your score is 0, in 12 turns.","","Would you like to RESTART, RESTORE a saved game, UNDO your last turn, or QUIT?"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every input line goes to that prompt until the player picks an exit — the four answers reuse the meta-verbs above, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"undo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the prompt revives on the turn before the fatal one, and a failed restore re-offers the prompt rather than stranding a dead world. Death from a timer body follows the same shape as death from a rule.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A dead world’s time has stopped: each-turn rules and timers no longer run. Internally that state is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameStatus\/dead","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — “over, but the conversation continues” — which is why a driver loops on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TurnResult.isFinished"},{"text":" rather than checking the status itself.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-resurrection-hook","text":"The resurrection hook","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A game can intercept every death by implementing ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game\/onDeath()","type":"reference"},{"text":". It runs the instant the player dies — after the ","type":"text"},{"code":"die(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" message prints, but ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the banner and prompt — and inside the live turn, so it can do anything a rule can: print prose, move the player, dock the score, scatter their belongings, bump a death counter. What it returns decides the death’s fate:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["func onDeath() -> DeathOutcome {","    deaths += 1","    for item in player.inventory { item.move(to: forest) }","    player.score -= 10","    player.location = forest","    say(\"A shadowy figure sets you down at the edge of the forest.\")","    return .consumed          \/\/ the player lives; play continues","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DeathOutcome\/consumed"},{"text":" revives the player: the world stays ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameStatus\/playing","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", the turn finishes normally (its fuses and daemons still tick), and no banner or prompt appears. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DeathOutcome\/fallThrough"},{"type":"text","text":" — the default — runs the standard death path unchanged, so a game that doesn’t implement "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDeath()"},{"type":"text","text":" dies exactly as before. This is how Zork models canonical resurrection: a toll and a teleport for the first few deaths, then a fall-through once the player has used up their luck."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UNDO"},{"type":"text","text":" after a consumed death rewinds the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"whole"}]},{"type":"text","text":" fatal turn — the death, the resurrection, and everything the handler did — back to where the player stood before it, which is the coherent thing to undo."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The worked examples","level":2,"anchor":"The-worked-examples","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For a small, readable pass at these mechanics on their own, the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Lighthouse","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" example ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Lighthouse\/"},{"type":"text","text":") has an oil lamp that burns down on two fuses (relighting restarts them) and a tide that rises on a daemon and drowns a player who lingers on the jetty — with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LighthouseTranscriptTests"},{"type":"text","text":" driving both."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"The lantern and the grue","type":"heading","anchor":"The-lantern-and-the-grue"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Zork1\/"},{"type":"text","text":" ties it together. The brass lantern is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lightSource"},{"text":" whose fuel is two fuses — a dim warning at 20 burning turns, dead at 25 — started by an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(.turnOn)"},{"text":" rule and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"paused"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" by ","type":"text"},{"code":"after(.turnOff)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (bank "},{"code":"fuseRemaining","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", stop the fuses; relighting restarts them at the banked counts). The grue is an autostarted daemon that counts consecutive turns ending in darkness: a warning, a silent turn of grace, then ","type":"text"},{"code":"die(…)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — and any lit turn resets it. Both survive save\/restore because their state is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the timer schedule.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Zork points the warning and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/pitchBlack","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" at the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"same"}]},{"type":"text","text":" sentence, because there the dark-room line is the threat — so on the turn you walk into the dark, the room describer and the grue both want to say it. Both reach for "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/sayOnceThisTurn(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", so the player reads it once, whichever spoke first. A game that words its dark room and its warning differently gets both lines, unchanged: the comparison is the text, not the situation."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"See also","level":2,"anchor":"See-also"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextAndRandomness","type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Light sources that carry into dark rooms, fuses and daemons that tick the world’s clock, saving and undoing, and killing the player without ending the program."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/darknesstimeanddeath"]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"title":"Darkness, Time, and Death","roleHeading":"Article"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/startDaemon(_:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Starts the named daemon; it first runs at the end of the current turn."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startDaemon(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"startDaemon"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"startDaemon(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/startdaemon(_:)"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/isLit":{"title":"isLit","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isLit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lightSource"},{"type":"text","text":" item is currently lit. Reads false — and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"assigning is a no-op — for anything that isn’t a light source. The"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"raw setter changes only the light itself; it never describes the room","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or announces the change (the ","type":"text"},{"code":"turn on","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"turn off","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" default actions do","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that).","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/islit","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isLit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Game/onDeath()":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/game\/ondeath()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game\/onDeath()","required":true,"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Called the instant the player dies — after the ","type":"text"},{"code":"die(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" message","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prints, but ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the death banner and the RESTART \/ RESTORE \/"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UNDO \/ QUIT prompt."}],"defaultImplementations":1,"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"onDeath()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"onDeath","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DeathOutcome","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto12DeathOutcomeO"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/stopDaemon(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/stopdaemon(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopDaemon(_:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stops the named daemon. A no-op if it isn’t running."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"stopDaemon(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"stopDaemon"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/fuse(_:after:autostart:perform:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declares a fuse: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" runs once, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"turns"},{"type":"text","text":" turns after the fuse is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"started — by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"startFuse(_:after:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in a rule, or from turn one with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"autostart"},{"type":"text","text":". Starting a running fuse resets its count."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/fuse(_:after:autostart:perform:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fuse","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"after","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"autostart","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"perform","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Void","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimedEvent","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto10TimedEventV"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"fuse(_:after:autostart:perform:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/fuse(_:after:autostart:perform:)"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/REPL":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/REPL","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/repl","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The outer loop: prompt → parse → perform → print, until the game ends or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"input runs out. Holds the only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" in a Gnusto game."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"REPL","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"REPL","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"REPL","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/IOHandler":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IOHandler","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the game’s text goes and player input comes from. Synchronous by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"design: a blocking console read is fine for a CLI; an async variant can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be added later without breaking this protocol’s clients."}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IOHandler","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IOHandler","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"IOHandler","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/iohandler"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameStatus/playing":{"title":"GameStatus.playing","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameStatus\/playing","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gamestatus\/playing","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"playing"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/DeathOutcome/consumed":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DeathOutcome\/consumed","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/deathoutcome\/consumed","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Swallow the death: the world stays "},{"code":".playing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the turn ends normally","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(its fuses and daemons still tick), and no death banner or prompt is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shown. The handler is responsible for making the continuation sensible","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"— teleporting the player somewhere alive, scattering their belongings,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"docking the score. Zork’s canonical resurrection."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"DeathOutcome.consumed","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"consumed"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/lightSource":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lightSource"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9ItemTraitV","text":"ItemTrait"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/lightsource","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/lightSource","title":"lightSource","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The item can hold light. It "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"starts unlit"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" unless it also declares"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"startsLit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; the player operates it with "},{"code":"turn on","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"turn off","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"light","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"extinguish","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), and rules can flip "},{"code":"item.isLit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" directly. While lit,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it lights the room it is in — carried by the player, lying in the room, on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a surface, or inside an open or "},{"code":"transparent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" container. There is no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"separate “always burning” trait: refuse "},{"code":".turnOff","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a rule to make a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"torch inextinguishable."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameStatus/dead":{"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dead","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gamestatus\/dead","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameStatus\/dead","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The player has died. Over, but not final: the world’s time has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stopped, yet the program keeps reading — the death prompt offers"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"RESTART \/ RESTORE \/ UNDO \/ QUIT."}],"title":"GameStatus.dead","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/sayOnceThisTurn(_:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"sayOnceThisTurn"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/sayoncethisturn(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/sayOnceThisTurn(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Prints a message unless this turn has already printed exactly it.","type":"text"}],"title":"sayOnceThisTurn(_:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText/pitchBlack":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"pitchBlack"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"GameText","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Line","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV4LineV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"GameText","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Nothing","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV7NothingV"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/pitchBlack","title":"pitchBlack","abstract":[{"text":"Looking around a dark room. The line most likely to want","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Line\/live(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":": it prints on every dark turn, in every dark room, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a game whose darkness has anything in it — a companion, a sound, a smell","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"— has to check that the thing is still there before saying so.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext\/pitchblack","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText/Line/live(_:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"live","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GameText","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Line","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV4LineV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Object","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext\/line\/live(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Line\/live(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A line that is assembled when it prints rather than when it is written."}],"title":"live(_:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TimedEvent":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/timedevent","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A named timed event, declared in a game or bundle "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timers"},{"type":"text","text":" block: a fuse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(fires once, N turns after it is started) or a daemon (runs at the end of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every turn while active). The body is registered at bootstrap and never"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"serialized; only the schedule — name → turns remaining, or the active","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"flag — lives in ","type":"text"},{"code":"WorldState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it saves and restores like any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state and a restore re-binds it to the declared body by name.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TimedEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"TimedEvent","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimedEvent","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/dark":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/dark","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/dark","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The location has no light of its own; it is dark unless lit by author code","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"room.isLit = true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") or by a light-providing item. Locations default to lit.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"dark","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dark"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto13LocationTraitV","text":"LocationTrait"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WritingRules":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach game logic to items, locations, and the world."}],"title":"Writing Rules","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/writingrules"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TheTurnPipeline":{"abstract":[{"text":"What happens between the player pressing Return and the next prompt.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"The Turn Pipeline","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/theturnpipeline"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/die(_:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"die","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Never","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5NeverO"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/die(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/die(_:)","title":"die(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Kills the player: prints the message, then the game’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game\/onDeath()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"handler runs. Unless that handler consumes the death (resurrection), the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"engine prints the death banner, reports the score, and offers RESTART \/","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"RESTORE \/ UNDO \/ QUIT — the program keeps running until the player picks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an exit. Distinct from ","type":"text"},{"code":"end(won:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which finishes the game outright.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/end(won:)":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/end(won:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Ends the game. The engine prints the final score after the turn’s output.","type":"text"}],"title":"end(won:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"end"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"won"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5NeverO","text":"Never"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/end(won:)"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","title":"Gnusto","abstract":[{"text":"A Swift engine for writing parser-driven interactive fiction — text adventures in the tradition of Zork and Infocom’s ZIL.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/isDaemonActive(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/isdaemonactive(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/isDaemonActive(_:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Whether the named daemon is currently active.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"isDaemonActive(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isDaemonActive","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TextAndRandomness":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/textandrandomness","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextAndRandomness","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Re-skin the engine’s stock lines, and roll dice that replay."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Text and Randomness"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/daemon(_:autostart:perform:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Declares a daemon: ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs at the end of every turn while the daemon","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is active — from ","type":"text"},{"code":"startDaemon(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a rule, or from turn one with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"autostart","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/daemon(_:autostart:perform:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"daemon","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"autostart","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"perform","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Void","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimedEvent","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto10TimedEventV"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"daemon(_:autostart:perform:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/daemon(_:autostart:perform:)"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/DeathOutcome/fallThrough":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"fallThrough","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DeathOutcome\/fallThrough","type":"topic","title":"DeathOutcome.fallThrough","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Let the standard death path run: the banner prints and the player is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"offered RESTART \/ RESTORE \/ UNDO \/ QUIT. The default."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/deathoutcome\/fallthrough"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/ScriptedIOHandler":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScriptedIOHandler"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/scriptediohandler","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ScriptedIOHandler","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Feeds a fixed list of commands and records everything into a transcript —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for tests and automated playthroughs. Ships in the library because game"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authors want transcript tests too."}],"title":"ScriptedIOHandler","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScriptedIOHandler"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location/isLit":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isLit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/isLit","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the location currently has light — its own (locations declared"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"dark","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" start unlit; all others start lit) or a lit "},{"code":"lightSource","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" item"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shining here. Read and write are deliberately asymmetric: the getter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answers “is there light here”, the setter gives or removes the room’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"inherent","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" light and never touches any item’s lit state."}],"title":"isLit","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location\/islit","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/stopFuse(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Stops the named fuse; it will not fire. A no-op if it isn’t running.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopFuse(_:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stopFuse","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"stopFuse(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/stopfuse(_:)"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/startFuse(_:after:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/startfuse(_:after:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startFuse(_:after:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Starts (or restarts, resetting the count of) the named fuse. "},{"code":"turns","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"overrides the declared count for this run. Naming an undeclared timer, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a daemon, is a programmer error and traps."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"startFuse(_:after:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"startFuse","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"after","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/fuseRemaining(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/fuseremaining(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/fuseRemaining(_:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How many end-of-turn ticks remain before the named fuse fires — "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when it isn’t running."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"fuseRemaining(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fuseRemaining"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}}}